      en: "The Anseba Valley is located in the Maekel region and extends along the Anseba River, which is 400 kilometers long. The valley is 10-20 kilometers wide and lies at an elevation of 1,500 to 2,000 meters. It is used for agriculture, mainly fruit trees and vegetables. Average temperature is 20 °C. Annual rainfall is 500-600 mm. Population density is about 100 per km². The city of Keren lies in the valley and has 60,000 inhabitants. The river is seasonal.",
